{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Sports and Leisure"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The First Olympic Games"}, {"type": "position", "content": 1}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Describe detailed facts about events or actions in work and social contexts, in written or spoken situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Understands general and detailed information, including specialized articles of the professional or academic life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Understands general and detailed information, including specialized articles of the professional or academic life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands general and detailed information, including specialized articles of the professional or academic life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands general and detailed information, including specialized articles of the professional or academic life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands general and detailed information, including specialized articles of the professional or academic life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le02ob01re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Adjectives to Describe Feelings and Character Traits."}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use adjectives to describe the feelings and characteristics of a person.<br/> Adjectives ending in <span class=\"strong\">-ing</span> are used to describe the characteristics of a person, thing or situation.<br/> Adjectives ending in <span class=\"strong\">-ed</span> are used to describe the feelings or emotions of a person. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Adjectives ending in <span class=\"strong\">-ed</span> can only be used to describe feelings or emotions. They describe how a person feels. They cannot be used to describe an object or situation.<br/> Adjectives ending in <span class=\"strong\">-ing</span> can be used either with a person or a situation. They describe the characteristics of a person or a situation. They also describe how a situation makes you feel. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Compare the differences:<br/> <ul><li>John is bored. (John feels bored)<br/> <li>John is boring. (John is a boring person)<br/> <li>The movie is boring. (The movie causes people to feel bored)<br/></li></ul> You cannot say the movie is bored, since the subject is not a person."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>I was <span class=\"strong\">shocked</span> by how <span class=\"strong\">shocking</span> the accident was yesterday.<br/> <li>John was <span class=\"strong\">confused</span> by the <span class=\"strong\">confusing</span> street signs in the city.<br/> <li>This gym class is <span class=\"strong\">tiring</span>. I feel really <span class=\"strong\">tired</span> right now.<br/> <li>The speech was really <span class=\"strong\">inspiring</span>! I feel <span class=\"strong\">inspired</span> to do more with my life now.</li></ul></span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "The games would be quite <span class=\"strong\">shocking</span>, as the athletes competed completely nude."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Wouldn't you be <span class=\"strong\">shocked</span> to see a unclothed boxing bout?"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Simple Past Passive"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the active voice when you want the \u2018doer' of the action to be the subject.<br/> You use the passive voice when you want the \u2018receiver' of the action to be the subject."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Most of spoken English uses active speech. In active sentences, the subject is the focus of the sentence.<br/> Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>The Romans (subject) <span class=\"strong\">stopped</span> the Olympic Games (object) in 396 AD. </li></ul></span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "A passive sentence puts the emphasis on the object of the active sentence. It now becomes the subject and focus of the passive sentence.<br/> Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>The Olympic Games (subject) <span class=\"strong\">were stopped by</span> the Romans (object)  in 396 AD.</li></ul></span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "It is not always necessary to mention the object in a passive sentence."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You make the passive form of a verb by using tenses of the <span class=\"italic\">be</span>  verb followed by the past participle. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The Simple Present passive form is:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "is/are + past participle"}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>The Olympic Games <span class=\"strong\">are celebrated</span> every four years.<br/> <li>Professional athletes <span class=\"strong\">are allowed</span> to participate in the modern Olympic Games.</li></ul></span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the Simple Present passive to talk about a situation that goes on in the present."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<br/>The Simple Past passive form is:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "was/were + past participle"}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>The Olympic Games <span class=\"strong\">were resumed</span> in 1896 in Greece.<br/> <li>The Games <span class=\"strong\">were held</span> every 4 years until 1994.</li></ul></span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the Simple Past passive to talk about a situation that is finished."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Women were forbidden from participating or even watching."}, {"type": "example", "content": "In 396 AD, the Olympic Games were stopped by the Roman emperor."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "amateur"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "describes an athlete who is not professional"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They were held every four years, and only amateur athletes were included."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le02ob01aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about competition."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "spectator "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who watches an activity or event"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Modern spectators would experience a number of confusing emotions watching the ancient games."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le02ob01aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "onlooker"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "someone who watches what is happening "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  A contemporary onlooker might also feel confused, because the rules governing the ancient events would be much different."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le02ob01aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "bout "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a match or combat"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Wouldn't you be shocked to see a clothesless boxing bout?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le02ob01aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to compete"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to try to win a sporting activity or event"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Some might find it particularly disgusting to know that athletes covered themselves in olive oil before competing."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le02ob01aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "counterpart"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something that has the same purpose as something else in a different place"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The ancient events would be much different than their modern counterparts."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le02ob01aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "idol"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who is very respected or admired"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The athletes with the most inspiring performances at the Olympic Games were treated as heroic idols."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le02ob01aud07"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go online and research a past Olympic Games."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a medal chart highlighting which countries won the most medals. Include your country."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Highlight the best individual performances of the games."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Present the results to your partner. "}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I research past events."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make a rankings chart."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I highlight inspiring performances."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my findings with a partner."}]}], "labs": [{"type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "id": 0, "exercises": [{"type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about leisure time, culture and sports."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can describe people, events or things. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can report facts about events and actions."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " How many medals did your country win at the last Olympic Games? Did you watch the last Olympics?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What's the highest level at which you have competed at sports?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type"