type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0}, {"type": "audio", "title": "", "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn10le02ob01re2img01.jpg", "text": "", "id": 0}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn10le02ob01re2img01.jpg", "text": "Did you know that the first Olympic Games took place in Greece in 776 BC? That's a pretty long time ago! The games included events such as racing, boxing, horse racing, and long jumping. They were held every four years, and only amateur athletes were included.", "id": 1}, {"time": "19000", "image": "engenn10le02ob01re2img02.jpg", "text": "It has been said that some events in the present-day Olympic games can be a bit boring. Modern spectators would experience a number of confusing emotions watching the ancient games, but they certainly wouldn't feel bored. First of all, the games would be quite shocking, as the athletes competed completely nude. Wouldn't you be shocked to see a unclothed boxing bout? Some might find it particularly disgusting to know that athletes covered themselves in olive oil before competing. A contemporary onlooker might also feel confused, because the rules governing the ancient events would be much different than their modern counterparts (some events were contested to the death, for example). Lastly, most people would certainly be more than a little bit disgusted to find that women were forbidden from participating or even watching.", "id": 2}, {"time": "69000", "image": "engenn10le02ob01re2img03.jpg", "text": "The athletes with the most inspiring performances at the Olympic Games were treated as heroic idols and were mentioned in songs and poems. However, when the games started turning into professional games, they lost their popularity. <br/>In 396 AD, the Olympic Games were stopped by the Roman emperor. They were not continued until 1896 when the modern Olympic Games began once more in Athens, Greece.<br/>The modern Olympic games were held every four years until 1994. Nowadays, they are held every two years, alternating between summer and winter games. Another change that started in the early 90s is that in some cases, professional athletes were allowed to participate.", "id": 3}], "audiosrc": "engenn10le02ob01re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le02ob01re2img01.jpg"}}], "id": 1}]}]}